From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:58:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Draw a frame on the home and the game lists only when it
 changes

- With RenderOnChange (default true) and only the view on the stack, the
  renderer keeps the frame's drawing as commands instead of sending them.
  At the frame's end they are sent and shown only when they differ from the
  frame on screen, or use a texture changed since (a video's new frame), and
  at least once a second; otherwise the screen keeps its frame and the main
  loop waits for the next frame's time or an event, so input is answered at
  once. Texture changes, read-backs (shaders, blur) and swaps inside a frame
  send what was kept first: the order of the drawing never changes.
- RenderOnChangeVerify draws every frame, reads it back, and logs a frame
  the cache would have left out whose pixels changed (for tests);
  DrawFramerate also shows the frames drawn per second.
